# chunk-read-out-of-range: pins that reading text out of range gives empty
# text and never raises: past the end, at index 0, before the start and over
# a reversed range (chapter 4, Reading). A range's ends are read as indexes
# first, then a range that isn't reversed is clipped to the Characters it
# covers, at either end: 2..10 gives "bc" and -5..2 gives "ab". -1..1 is 3..1,
# so it is reversed. A list read out of range gives Nothing for one item and
# an empty list for a range. No `raise` record is written.
# Fuel, allocation and state figures are estimates.
# Unblessed: the output lines are written by hand, not by bless.

> load reads
> deliver d1 to=reads message=go
> pump clock=2026-09-30T09:00:00Z
seg reads/r1 start delivery=d1 handler=go clause=1 fuel=116 alloc=64 state=100 end=return
run reads/r1 outcome=completed delivery=d1 handler=go fuel=116 alloc=64
pumped state=idle fuel=116

> vars
vars reads pastEnd="" wordZero="" itemPastEnd="" beforeStart="" reversed="" overhang="bc" underhang="ab" wrapsReversed="" wholeRangePast="" listPastEnd=nothing listRangePast=[]
